{"id": "EUVD-2026-103028", "enisaUuid": "45f0a896-2894-3bef-9962-cd78d14717a1", "description": "Huly Platform through 0.7.432 contains a missing authorization vulnerability that allows any authenticated user to merge arbitrary persons by calling the mergeSpecifiedPersons account RPC. Attackers knowing two person UUIDs can graft attacker-controlled unverified social ids onto a victim person, then use login or password recovery to take over the victim account.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:38:47", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T21:19:52", "baseScore": 8.6, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/huly-platform-merge-specified-persons-missing-authorization", "https://github.com/hcengineering/platform/issues/10914", "https://github.com/hcengineering/platform/blob/v0.7.432/server/account/src/operations.ts#L2921-L2939", "https://github.com/hcengineering/platform/commit/afe11faec1b56f278c0882355a69b08cff1eebd9", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/huly-platform-through-0.7.432-account-takeover-via-mergespecifiedpersons-rpc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111606", "GHSA-8cm6-vrv9-4v98"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f6d43087-5677-35b5-b67b-937d286073b6", "product": {"name": "Huly Platform", "vendor": {"name": "hcengineering"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.7.432"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9f2ffbed-1cd1-3605-878d-62780ffa9144", "vendor": {"name": "hcengineering"}}], "isExploited": false}